    "title": "Top 10 Metal Drummers' Signature Snare Drums",
    "description": "Every list on MetalForge until now has ranked drummers by genre — this is the site's first list built around gear instead: the most notable named signature snare drums drummers have co-designed with manufacturers, the rare tier of gear partnership where a company builds and markets a drum around one player's specific tonal and mechanical requirements rather than simply putting that player's name on an existing catalog model. A true signature snare is a career milestone most working drummers never reach — it requires enough commercial standing for a manufacturer to commit tooling and marketing to a bespoke shell, and it typically documents exactly what that drummer needed from a snare that the existing catalog could not provide. Metallica's Lars Ulrich set the modern template with Tama's LU1465, a 14x6.5\" model that has anchored his kit since the 1990s, while Slipknot's Joey Jordison's Pearl 13x6.5\" signature became one of the most recognized snare silhouettes in metal specifically because of its unusually shallow depth for the genre. This list ranks the ten most significant metal drummer signature snares by the drum's design impact, commercial longevity, and the tonal identity it created — physical objects that document a decade or more of a working relationship between drummer and manufacturer.",
