    "title": "Top 10 Metal Drummers Who Also Produce & Engineer",
    "description": "MetalForge's drummer database documents dozens of players' recorded output — but a small subset of that roster didn't stop at performing. This list ranks the drummers whose career extends behind the board: producing, engineering, or otherwise shaping recordings beyond their own drum parts, a distinct skill set from performance that requires understanding arrangement, mix balance, and other musicians' instruments well enough to guide a finished record. Dream Theater's Mike Portnoy built one of metal's most extensive producer credits across his own catalog and beyond; Slipknot's Joey Jordison carried a \"record producer\" credit throughout his career alongside his drumming; and Obscura's Hannes Grossmann runs his own studio in Germany, producing and mixing metal albums for other bands between his own recording cycles. The list also includes drummers whose production work moved outside metal entirely — Sepultura's Igor Cavalera as an electronic music producer with Mixhell, and Death's Richard Christy, who left metal drumming behind for a second career producing for radio. Each entry below is a documented production or engineering credit drawn directly from that drummer's own career record, not a hypothetical extension of their drumming reputation.",
