    "description": "Blast beats and groove usually sit at opposite ends of metal drumming, but a select group of extreme metal players have found the pocket inside the chaos — the Gojira and Behemoth school of drumming that keeps death and black metal's speed and aggression while making a listener's head nod instead of just recoil. This list ranks the drummers who built genuinely extreme metal careers around a groove sensibility, distinct from pure blast-beat specialists and from the mid-tempo groove metal tradition that never touches extreme metal's technical ceiling.",
